=begin pod :kind("Type") :subkind("class") :category("basic")

=TITLE class RakuAST::Name::Part::EmptyEdge

=SUBTITLE Represent an empty part at the start/end of a Name

    class RakuAST::Name::Part::EmptyEdge { }

The C<RakuAST::Name::Part::EmptyEdge> class represents an empty part of
a L<C<RakuAST::Name>|/type/RakuAST/Name> object as either the first or
last part of the name.

=head2 Object introspection

C<RakuAST::Name::Part::EmptyEdge> object is typically created when
parsing Raku Programming Language code.  So most developers will only
need to know how to introspect the objects created.

=head3 name

=begin code :preamble<my $part>
dd $part.name;  # ""
=end code

Returns the name of this part.  Is always the empty string.

=head3 is-empty

=begin code :preamble<my $part>
say $part.names-empty;  # True
=end code

Returns whether this is an empty part of a C<RakuAST::Name>.  Always
returns C<True>.

=head3 is-pseudo-package

=begin code :preamble<my $part>
say $part.is-pseudo-package;  # False
=end code

Returns whether this part could be considered a pseudo-package.  Always
returns C<False>.

=head2 Object creation

=begin code
my $part = RakuAST::Name::Part::Empty.new;
=end code

A C<RakuAST::Name::Part::EmptyEdge> object is instantiated with the
C<.new> method, which does B<not> take any arguments.

=end pod
